From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:22:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] thunderbolt: apple: Optionally allow CL states on
 T8132

The T8132 ACIO keeps its links in CL0 (no_host_clx), because a link
retrained shortly after CL states were enabled. A link that can never
enter CL0s, CL1 or CL2 keeps its lanes fully powered whenever a USB4 or
Thunderbolt device is attached, also while nothing crosses it. macOS
records a CLx state for every lane adapter of these routers.

Add host_clx (read-only, default N). With it set, the NHI does not take
QUIRK_NO_HOST_CLX on such a generation, and the core enables CL states as
it does on other USB4 hosts. This lets a test measure again whether the
retraining still happens and what the CL states save at idle. A warning
records that it is on.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/thunderbolt/apple.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/thunderbolt/apple.c b/drivers/thunderbolt/apple.c
index e90e22c3b6..c05f61140b 100644
--- a/drivers/thunderbolt/apple.c
+++ b/drivers/thunderbolt/apple.c
@@ -334,6 +334,16 @@ MODULE_PARM_DESC(dpin_mode_value,
 /* DP IN adapters without an interrupt are polled this often (ms). */
 #define APPLE_DPIN_POLL_MS 20
 
+/*
+ * Some ACIO generations keep their links in CL0 (no_host_clx): on T8132 a
+ * link retrained shortly after CL states were enabled. This lets a test run
+ * the CL states there again, from the next NHI probe.
+ */
+static bool host_clx;
+module_param(host_clx, bool, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(host_clx,
+		 "Allow CL link power states on ACIO generations that keep their links in CL0 (T8132; default N; experimental)");
+
 static bool cio_s2r;
 module_param(cio_s2r, bool, 0400);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(cio_s2r, "Enable experimental J713/J604 attached-dock system sleep");
@@ -2526,8 +2536,10 @@ static int apple_nhi_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	anhi->nhi.quirks = QUIRK_NO_DMA_PORT | QUIRK_NO_USB3_BW_ALLOC;
 	if (anhi->nhi.host_dp_policy)
 		anhi->nhi.quirks |= QUIRK_HOST_DP_NFC_CREDITS;
-	if (acio->hw->no_host_clx)
+	if (acio->hw->no_host_clx && !host_clx)
 		anhi->nhi.quirks |= QUIRK_NO_HOST_CLX;
+	else if (acio->hw->no_host_clx)
+		dev_warn(anhi->dev, "host_clx: CL states allowed on this ACIO (experimental)\n");
 	if (acio->hw->no_asym)
 		anhi->nhi.quirks |= QUIRK_NO_ASYM;
 	if (acio->hw->gen4_link_recovery)
-- 
